        "comparator_sha256": "6c69569b984736453a87ae5751c1fba71799f71c4cba0fce9f07683bab694565",
        "explanation": "Table 6.1 row 1 (-\u00a32,625m) covers more than the payment we model, \u00a3100 to households in council tax bands A to D in England only. Budget 2026 paragraph 3.5: \"a \u00a32.6 billion Household Energy Payment ... \u00a3100 payment for households in bands A-D in England from January 2027. The devolved governments will receive their share of funding through the Barnett formula, which will enable them to provide similar support.\" Paragraph 3.6: \"this Budget provides \u00a3100 million additional funding for local authorities in England to provide further targeted support to households acutely impacted by rising energy bills, some of whom are in council tax bands above A-D.\" Neither the Barnett share nor the \u00a3100m is modelled; the policy costings document has no page for this measure, so the split of the \u00a32.6bn is not published. Ours, -\u00a31.969bn, is about 20 million households at \u00a3100 (paragraph 3.5's \"up to 20 million households\"). Decided by Vahid, 28 October 2026. Refreshed to the final artifact (101a07dc7238a10e).",
